    <img src={heroImage} alt="HOSHANHO Japanese-style chef knife" loading="lazy" />
    <div><p class="hh-guide-kicker">01 / EVERYDAY PREP</p><h3>Chef knife or Gyuto</h3><p>A chef knife or Japanese-style Gyuto is often the most versatile starting point for slicing, chopping and mincing. Compare blade length, weight, balance, handle shape and whether the edge profile suits your cutting technique.</p><a href={affiliate('https://www.hoshanho.com/collections/1-piece')} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer">Explore individual knives ↗</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="hh-guide-feature">
    <img src={nakiriImage} alt="HOSHANHO Nakiri vegetable knife" loading="lazy" />
    <div><p class="hh-guide-kicker">02 / VEGETABLE PREP</p><h3>Nakiri</h3><p>A Nakiri has a tall, generally straight-edged blade designed for vegetable preparation. Its shape can be useful for controlled up-and-down chopping and push cuts. It is not a substitute for a heavy cleaver or a pointed chef knife for every task.</p><a href={affiliate('https://www.hoshanho.com/products/7-nakiri-knife-japanese-steel')} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer">View the HOSHANHO Nakiri listing ↗</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="hh-guide-feature">
    <img src={heroImage} alt="HOSHANHO Japanese-style kitchen knife" loading="lazy" />
    <div><p class="hh-guide-kicker">03 / SLICING & SMALL TASKS</p><h3>Santoku, paring and bread knives</h3><p>A Santoku is a general-purpose option for slicing, dicing and mincing. A paring knife is better suited to small, controlled tasks such as peeling and trimming. A serrated bread knife helps cut through crusts without compressing softer interiors. Choose based on the foods you prepare most often.</p><a href={affiliate('https://www.hoshanho.com/collections/santoku-knife')} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer">Explore Santoku knives ↗</a></div>
