  </div>
  <p>Also consider cutting boards, honing tools and protective sheaths where available. A board should provide a stable work surface and be maintained according to its material. A honing rod is intended to realign an edge between sharpening sessions; it does not replace sharpening when a blade has become dull.</p>

  <h2 id="buying">What to compare before buying HOSHANHO knives</h2>
  <div class="hh-guide-checks">
    <section><strong>01 · Steel and construction</strong><p>Check the exact steel description, layered construction if stated, hardness range and any heat-treatment details published for that model.</p></section>
    <section><strong>02 · Blade shape and length</strong><p>Match the profile and dimensions to the foods you prepare, your cutting board and your preferred technique.</p></section>
    <section><strong>03 · Handle and balance</strong><p>Review handle material, shape, grip and overall dimensions. Comfort is personal, so check return terms if you are unsure.</p></section>
    <section><strong>04 · Included pieces</strong><p>For sets, verify every blade, block, sheath, sharpener or accessory included in the exact bundle.</p></section>
    <section><strong>05 · Storage and care</strong><p>Check whether storage is included and read the model-specific cleaning, drying and maintenance instructions.</p></section>
    <section><strong>06 · Returns and warranty</strong><p>Review current coverage, exclusions, return window and any conditions before ordering.</p></section>
