  <h2 id="care">Knife care and maintenance basics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Clean and dry promptly:</strong> follow the manufacturer's care directions and dry the blade thoroughly after washing. Do not assume a knife is dishwasher-safe unless the exact listing says so.</li>
    <li><strong>Use an appropriate cutting surface:</strong> a suitable wood or plastic board is generally kinder to an edge than hard surfaces such as glass, stone or ceramic.</li>
    <li><strong>Store blades safely:</strong> use a sheath, block, drawer insert or magnetic holder that securely supports the knife and protects the edge.</li>
    <li><strong>Hone and sharpen as needed:</strong> honing can help maintain alignment; sharpening removes material to restore an edge. Use a method appropriate for the knife's edge and steel.</li>
    <li><strong>Handle with care:</strong> keep sharp knives away from loose drawers and never leave a blade hidden in soapy water.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Always defer to the care instructions supplied with the specific knife. Different steels, finishes, handles and construction methods may have different maintenance requirements.</p>

