  <h2 id="faq">HOSHANHO buying guide questions</h2>
  <h3>Is a Japanese-style chef knife the same as a Santoku?</h3><p>No. Both can be versatile kitchen knives, but their blade profiles and typical dimensions differ. Compare the exact shape and length and choose the one that suits your cutting style.</p>
  <h3>Is a Nakiri only for vegetables?</h3><p>A Nakiri is designed around vegetable preparation, especially chopping and push-cutting. It is not intended to replace every other kitchen knife.</p>
  <h3>Should I buy a knife set or individual knives?</h3><p>Choose a set when you will use most of its included pieces and value the coordinated storage. Choose individual knives when you know which blades you need and want to avoid extras.</p>
  <h3>Are HOSHANHO knives dishwasher-safe?</h3><p>Do not assume so. Follow the care instructions for the exact product and check its listing before cleaning.</p>
